<mxCell id="36" value="&lt;b&gt;DETAILED NOTE C-1: ERP AUTOMATED CREDIT LIMIT ENFORCEMENT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;ERP Validation Engine:&lt;/b&gt; The ERP acts as the frontline gatekeeper. Whenever operations or billing attempts to book a job code, the ERP cross-references the client ledger in real-time.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Two Blocking Triggers:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;  1. &lt;i&gt;Ageing Violation:&lt;/i&gt; Any unpaid invoice exceeding 30 days overdue immediately locks the client account.&lt;br/&gt;  2. &lt;i&gt;Exposure Ceiling:&lt;/i&gt; If the total exposure (unbilled jobs + outstanding invoices) exceeds the approved credit limit, the system refuses job creation.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Turnaround SLA:&lt;/b&gt; Authority matrix approval requests must be addressed within &lt;b&gt;1 working day&lt;/b&gt; to prevent operational cargo dispatch delays." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffdf5;strokeColor=#f59e0b;fontColor=#1c1917;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;arcSize=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1240" y="160" width="720" height="240" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="37" value="&lt;b&gt;DETAILED NOTE C-2: RISK ASSESSMENT &amp; ADVANCE SECURITY PDC MANDATE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Pre-requisites for Temporary Limit Enhancement:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;  - Head CC conducts a tripartite evaluation: creditworthiness history, strategic client relationship, and gross freight margin/business volume.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Mandatory Risk Mitigation (Security Cheques):&lt;/b&gt; The SOP strictly mandates collecting advance Post-Dated Cheques (PDC) or security deposit cheques covering the excess exposure prior to granting shipment approval.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Single Shipment vs Blanket Limit:&lt;/b&gt; Overrides are granted strictly on a per-shipment basis unless an institutional credit review is formally completed." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffdf5;strokeColor=#f59e0b;fontColor=#1c1917;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;arcSize=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1240" y="430" width="720" height="250" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
<mxCell id="38" value="&lt;b&gt;DETAILED NOTE C-3: DUAL-KEY GOVERNANCE &amp; MD/DIRECTOR APPROVAL&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Separation of Financial Powers:&lt;/b&gt; While Head CC can authorize operational shipment releases against security PDCs, they CANNOT unilaterally approve limit expansions funded by credit notes.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Credit Note Funding Exception:&lt;/b&gt; Any excess-limit request backed or funded via credit note adjustments introduces commercial dilution risk and strictly requires the signature of the &lt;b&gt;Managing Director / Directors&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Audit Trail:&lt;/b&gt; All overrides, approvals, and rejection notes are permanently logged in the ERP authorization log for statutory audit scrutiny." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fffdf5;strokeColor=#f59e0b;fontColor=#1c1917;fontSize=11;fontStyle=0;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;arcSize=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
  <mxGeometry x="1240" y="710" width="720" height="250" as="geometry" />
</mxCell>
  </root>
</mxGraphModel>